Well, Garett, I think that patches are very useful, because they:

	1 Use up less net bandwidth (approx. 5-10% of original sources)
	2 Can be distributed much faster than the original sources (size!)
	3 Form a reliable form of source updates, which is however to some
	  extent related to the experience and know-how of the people
	  applying the patches.

Personnally, I think Of-the-Wall software (patch and friends) form a major
enhancement of the Usenet usability. And... I never had severe problems with
patch; that's more than I can say about some `commercial' packages.
